From db780816d02f92fe4c0b14b43199d294b6055e08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:40:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 148/156] net: sparx5: offload the taprio qdisc
Organization: Wires

A time-aware shaper on a switch port gates only what the CPU sends;
the chip forwards everything else past the qdisc.

The driver sets the TAS link speed of a port but never programs a
gate control list.

Offload taprio to the TAS block.  The schedule goes to free gate
control list entries, one of the port's two lists points at them, and
the list starts at the base time moved into the future by whole
cycles, as the PSFP gates already do.  A new schedule replaces one
that has not started yet, and stops a running one when it starts.

SparX-5 keeps a list as a contiguous block and addresses its entries
from the base; LAN969x links each entry to the next and addresses
them from the start of the table, which has 3000 entries against the
10000 of SparX-5.  Both follow the vendor's MESA API[1], which the
vendor BSP kernel[2] does not on LAN969x.

Set-and-hold entries and the cycle time extension are refused, the
queue max SDU is left to the qdisc.

[1] https://github.com/microchip-ung/mesa/blob/master/base/fa/vtss_lan969x_tas.c
[2] https://github.com/microchip-ung/linux/tree/bsp-6.18-2026

Signed-off-by: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
